renewed prominence in recent days I urge
all parties to work together urgently to
pass these bills since September 11th our
border crossings have been on high state
of alert and security measures were
immediately increased at our airports
but in the days since it has become
clear that the scope of the threat that
terror poses to our way of life has no
parallel we in North America have been
extraordinarily fortunate to live in
peace untouched by attack but that has changed.
additional action is required from
Canada and all nations domestically and
in concert without each other for there
to be a truly effective and truly global
offensive against terrorism accordingly
mr. Speaker I am pleased to update the
house on the specific steps our
government is taking as part of a
comprehensive action plan on Canadian
security the plan whose goals are to
protect Canadian citizens keep our
borders secure protect our values
sustain our economy and defy the threat
of terrorism that terrorism poses to
free and civilised nations everywhere
our action plan entails quote immediate
action and new legislation it is
measured and focused and it equips
Canada to be an aggressive international
partner in the coalition to destroy
roots and branch the shadow networks of
supply finance and penetration that
allow the terrorists to carry out the
mass murder of September 11th above all
our plan will reassure Canadians that
even even in the wake of September 11 we
can live our
lives on our terms according to our
values not on terms dictated from the
shadows
but as I told a NATO Parliamentary
Assembly last week Mr Speaker we must be
clear in our minds that this is a new
kind of struggle against a new kind of
enemy and we must not allow ourselves to
be trapped by the rhetoric or
experiences of past Wars to define our
tactics or measure our success
the twisted calculus of success for our
adversaries is not total gain but the
extent to which they can through terror
ripped at the very fiber of our
societies disrupt our economies set
community against community faith
against faith or citizen against citizens
Monsieur le président, il ne fait aucun doute
que la pouvoir militaire jouer un rôle dans
le nouveau conflit. Ainsi, j’ai autorisé l’opération
Apollo, le déploiement militaire le plus étendu
du Canada depuis la guerre de Corée.
Plus de 2000 hommes et femmes participeront.
Des rôles essentiels ont été attribués à nos navires
à nos transporteurs aériens? (ou transport aérien, pas sûr),
et à nos avions de surveillance, dans le cadre de la campagne militaire
internationale contre Isama Ben Laden, son réseau, Al Quaeda
et le régime renégat des Taliban qui les héberge
en Afghanistan. Depuis le début de cette
campagne, nous avons dit très clairement
que nous ne ciblions pas l’islam,
mais plutôt un groupe d’extrémistes
dont le but est de terroriser
et de perturber les nations.
Ces actes meurtriers ont très
injustement terni la réputation
d’une grande religion mondiale, l’islam.
Nous ne sommes pas non plus en conflit
avec le peuple afghan.
En fait, le monde s'efforce de fournir
de l'aide aux Afghans.
Nous sommes en conflit
avec le régime des talibans.
Monsieur le Président, aucune
décision ne pourrait être aussi
grave pour un premier ministre
que d'envoyer des soldats canadiens
dans des opérations militaires.
Nous comprenons que tous
les Canadiens sont conscients
de la gravité de cette décision.

(Mr. Speaker, there is no doubt[?] military power will play a role in the new conflict. Thus, I have authorized operation Apollo, the most extensive military deployment for Canada since the Korean War. More than 2,000 men and women will take part. Vital roles have been assigned to our ships to our air craft carriers? (or air transport, not sure), and to our surveillance airplanes, as part of the international military campaign against Isama Bin Ladin his network, Al Quaeda and the renegade Taliban regime who harbours them in Afghanistan. From the beginning of this campaign, we have said very clearly, that we do not target Islam, but rather a group of extremists whose goal is to terrify and disrupt the nations. These murderous acts have very unfairly sullied the reputation of a great world religion, Islam. Neither are we at conflict with the Afghan people. In fact, the world is trying very hard to bring aid to the people of Afghanistan. We are in conflict with the Taliban regime.
Mr President, no decision could be as serious for a prime minister as sending Canadian soldiers to participate in military operations. We understand that all Canadians are conscious of the gravity of this decision.)

