Tajuk: Ucapan Jelajah Harapan Selamatkan Malaysia
15 April 2018 di Langkawi

Terima kasih. Terima kasih.
Assalamualaikum …... dan salam sejahtera kepada hadirin sekalian.
Yang Berhormat Dato Sri Wan Azizah, Presiden Parti Pakatan Harapan, Yang Berbahagia Tun Haji Mat Sabu, Yang Berhormat Tuan Haji Muhyiddin Yassin, Mukriz Mahathir, Encik Izzat.
Tuan tuan puan puan hadirin sekalian
Saya amat gembira pada malam ini kerana begitu ramai penduduk Langkawi datang ke majlis ceramah pakatan harapan
Saya yakin orang Langkawi pun tak nak tengok orang … ramai berkumpul di satu tempat untuk dengar syarahan-syarahan.
Saya tak pernah, tapi yang datang ini pun tak pernah juga. Ini kerana apa? Kerana saya yakin rakyat langkawi prihatin terhadap keadaan dalam negara kita, khususnya di langkawi
kerana kita berasa bertanggung jawab terhadap keadaan di negara kita. Kitalah yang bertanggung jawab bukan orang lain, dan kitalah yang akan menentukan sama ada negara kita ditadbir dengan baik ataupun tidak baik
Sepertimana kita tersemua faham, Negara kita memilih sistem demokrasi untuk menentukan kepimpinan kerajaan di malaysia
Sistem demokrasi ini memberi kuasa dan hak kepada rakyat tiap lima tahun ataupun empat tahun memilih siapa yang nak menjadi kerajaan
Yalah kadang kala kita tak buat tahu jenis manusia yang kita nak pilih tetapi kalau kita tahu tentulah kita lebih bijak (terima kasih)
Biasanya kita nak pilih orang yang kita tak kenal, kadang kala kita buat salah, pasal kita tak kenal dia. tetapi kalau kita dah tahu dia ini [...] dan kita pilih juga, siapa salah? Kitalah salah
Jadi sekarang ini ingat orang langkawi tahu ramai pemimpin pemimpin parti ini, jadi saya yakin orang langkawi akan pilih akan pilih yang terbaik bagi langkawi dan bagi negara kita malaysia.
Dan siapakah yang terbaik, susah nak tahulah
Tapi siapa yang [penjangak?]? Kita tahu, Najib. Yang kita tahu kita tak pilih najib, jangan pangkah
[... ataupun … itu]
Jangan juga pangkah bulan, bulan itu tak beberapa terang lah. tuan2puan2, Najib ini sebernanya penakut.
dia nak berlawan dalam pilihan raya ini dia nak berlawan, dia ingat dia boleh menang, tapi nak tentukan dia menang, dia cuba musnahkan musuh dia dulu. Ini macam orang lawan boxing. Bila nak lawan kena ikat tangan sebelah kawan nak lawan dengan dia, baru dia berani lawan. Ah Najib macam ini lah.
Dia nak lawan dengan kita, awal awal lagi dia haramkan parti kita
Dengan itu boleh menang tanpa bertanding. Ini tanda tanda orang pengecut, penyakut. Dulu kita tengok dalam negara kita ini, kerajaan kalau ada parti lawan, nak lawan dengan kerajaan ok, tak ada masalah nak daftar pun tak apa, nak lawan pun tak apa, nak pilih siapa pun tak apa, tetapi Najib ini, dia nak tentukan orang yang lawan diharamkan tak boleh bertanding supaya dia dapat kemenangan [6:37].
inilah yang saya kata, najib ini [bacol?], kalau dia berani, kepada parti pribumi ini bagi lah kita lawan. Dia tunggu sampai nak pilihan raya baru dia batal, sebelum ini kalau dia batal awal awal lagi kita pun boleh buat benda benda yang lain. tetapi walaupun dia batal parti kita ini di saat yang terakhir tetapi kita tahu macam mana nak susun diri kita, sebab itu hari ini saya bercakap di sini bukan dengan bendera merah.
Saya bercakap dengan bendera biru merah putih. Biarlah parti keadilan rakyat malaysia. Kenapa? Kerana kita tahu Najib ini dia hanya berani lawan pasal dia ada banyak parti parti yang sokong dia. Tiga parti, dalam barisan nasional, dia rasa beranilah. Tapi bila dia tengok parti parti lawan, sudah bergabung, nak buat satu parti pakatan harapan, maka dia berasa takut. Dia cari jalan supaya Pakatan Harapan ini tidak akan didaftar, dia tak nak daftar Pakatan Harapan, macam mana dia nak buat? Dia kata parti pribumi yang menjadi satu daripada anggota parti Pakatan Harapan ini melakukan kesalahan. [...nya 8:34] kita ada mesyuarat agung yang tak sah, tak sah bagi dialah, bagi kami sah. Tapi nak cari sebab, nak kata kami bersalah, supaya kita dapat niadaftarkan ataupun diharamkan, selepas kami diharamkan, maka parti Pakatan Harapan juga tak boleh ditubuhkan, tapi tak ada parti pribumi, tak ada parti harapan, Najib ingat dia boleh [...undi], tak nak lawan. Inilah orang yang pengecut, tapi kita tahu macam mana nak susun langkah untuk kita akan terus berperang dengan mereka. dan kita lihat ramai rakyat yang menyokong tindakan yang diambil oleh kita, iaitu walaupun tidak ada pendaftaran, bagi parti Pakatan Harapan tetapi kami masih bersatu dan kami bersetuju untuk mengguna hanya satu logo sahaja. Satu bendera sahaja. bendera Parti Keadilan Rakyat Malaysia. [9:58]
Fikir tengok lah, parti DAP ini 50 tahun dia bertanding di bawah logo roket. Tapi dia pun sanggup gugurkan roket pasal nak bertanding bersama dengan kami, supaya kita ada perpaduan dan kita berdiri sebagai satu parti dan kita tidak akan berlawan sesama sendiri. Parti Pakatan Harapan ini kami [empat?] parti di dalam satu satu kawasan akan letak hanya satu wakil, satu calon sahaja, kami tak nak letak 4-5 calon, satu daripada Amanah, satu daripada DAP, satu daripada Keadilan, satu daripada Pribumi. [...4] kita lawan sama ada dia lah menang. Tapi kami nak guna satu logo, dan satu saja calon, dalam tiap tiap kawasan pilihan raya. Di sini di langkawi ini kita akan letak satu calon bagi kawasan parlimen langkawi dan satu calon bagi kawasan state di Kuah dan di Ayer Hangat jadi tak ada berlawan sesama kita. Musuh kita ialah BN, dan musuh kecil kita ialah bulan. Saya kata musuh kecil pasal dia tahu dia tak boleh menang. Dia masuk [...] siapa? nak bagi Najib menang, nak tarik orang yang sokong kami, supaya Najib dapat lebih banyak salur undi [12:02] dan menang. jadi niat ini tak baik lah. Nak lawan lawan lah untuk diri sendiri, ini nak kecoh, nak masuk bertanding, kerana nak tolong Najib. kenapa nak tolong Najib? kerana dedak. Ini abdul kata dia dapat dedak, bapa nama hadi pun kata dia dapat dedak banyak.
Tuan-tuan puan-puan, kami tak perlu dedak, kami akan berusaha sedaya upaya walaupun Najib sekat tak bagi kami kutip duit, ada orang yang nak derma kepada kami. Maka mereka itu akan dilawati oleh LHDN lembaga hasil dalam negeri. Yang meminta mereka bayar lebih daripada cukai yang patut dibayar oleh mereka. Ada yang kena bayar 90 juta ringgit tambahan cukai. Tak ada sebab pun. Kata dia kalau tak bayar, kami akan senarai hitamkan kamu tak boleh keluar negeri kerana pasport dirampaskan sebagainya. Inilah cara Najib nak lawan dengan orang salah guna kuasa. Tuan-tuan puan-puan walaupun kami tak ada duit banyak tetapi kami dapat [punca bahu?] untuk kami guna lawan dengan Najib. Rupa-rupanya Najib ini dia suka bagi duit ke orang. Dia mari langkawi di bagi duit. Tiba-tiba orang dapat duit, dapat kereta pun, dapat motosikal pun, dapat [...13:58] rumah pun, dia bagi. Duit pun dia bagi. Tapi orang nyata duit itu dia bagi duit itu kat kami. Duit yang dia bagi kepada orang itu, duit itu dia bagi kami guna untuk nak lawan dengan Najib. Padan muka dia. Duit dia kita guna nak lawan bagi dia [tersemua?] Inilah Najib, dia ingat dia pandai sangat, dia kata “cash is king”. Ada duit saja bagi kat orang orang akan sokong. Orang tak sokong duit dia [terimalah? 14:38]. Tapi dia tak sokong, jadi bagi duit kat kita hantam Najib sekali. Ini Najib punya strategi tak makan. Orang Langkawi bukan nak sangat lah duit kamu itu, pasal duit itu duit dicuri. Ini [pengkhianat?] dia curi duit.
Inilah Najib. Macam macam cara dia buat pasal dia nak menang dan cara-cara dia semua cara menipu, kalau dia tak tipu, saya fikir tak ada [...] langsung kat Langkawi. Dia datang malam ini dia tengok orang ini semua … dia … dia tengok begitu ramai dia nanti [pilih?] tak paya bertanding lah. Berambil masa saja. Tuan-tuan puan-puan sebab itu dia nak tipu, dia buat macam-macam nak tipu, senarai pengundi pun dia kecoh. Dia tambah nama macam macam, 4 juta ahli penama undi tak ada alamat yang penuh. kita tak tahu dia duduk di mana. … dia duduk di atas langit, bila tak cukup dia turun lah, bagi undi kat Najib. Ada orang nama dia sampai 9 ... kali, nama semacam 9 … kali. IC kad pun kad semacam, umur pun semacam, duduk dia di Kedah, di Perlis, di Perak, di Selangor, di Johor, rupa-rupanya ada pakatan ibu bapa mereka ini pada satu hari nak lahir anak bersama sama bagi nama semacam. Inilah Najib. Tipu. Senarai pun dia tipu. Dia tipu pula [pekan?] antara kawasan kawasan pilihan raya. [Pekan?] dia ubah. Dia nak tolak supaya orang cina masuk kawasan lain, orang melayu kawasan lain. Kerana dia takut orang cina akan tolong orang melayu bagi kemenangan bagi Pakatan Harapan [17:13].
Ini adalah caranya, tapi saya fikir Orang Melayu yang dikumpul di kawasan dia pun tidak akan undi BN, akan undi Pakatan Harapan. Dia buat silap. Dia istihal, hari mengundi ialah pada hari rabu. Hari rabu, bukan hari cuti, jadi orang semua duduk kerja. Tiba-tiba dia sedar kalau buat pada hari yang bukan cuti, penyokong-penyokong BN pun tak boleh pergi undi juga, dia akan kalah. Sebab itulah dia bagi cuti, cuti seluruh negara pada hari Rabu, 9 hari bulan. Itulah nak tipu orang kena bertanggung diri sendiri.
Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan, saya yakin walau macam mana penipuan dilakukan pun, Najib tak akan menang kerana orang semua bila saya cakap, dengan siapa juga yang saya jumpa tak ada seorang pun yang nak Datuk Seri Najib. Inilah orangnya yang hari ini menjadi perdana menteri kita. Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan, kalau kita nak cari pemimpin, kita tak lah mencari pencuri untuk jadi pemimpin. Kita nak cari ah? No, pencuri! Tetapi dia sampai memalu kita macam cerita tadi. Bila pilihan negeri, orang tanya datang daripada mana? Kita kata Brunei. Takut, malu, pasal perdana menteri kita adalah seorang penjara.
Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan, kita saja yang boleh tentukan Najib punya penipuan ini tidak akan berkesan. Caranya ialah dengan pada hari mengundi, kita keluar beramai-ramai. Kita nak seberapa ramai pengundi akan keluar, undi Pakatan Harapan. Pasal kalau undi, kalau Pakatan Harapan menang cuma seratus dua ratui, Najib akan tipu pasal dia nampak ada cara orang daripada atas angin ini yang dia sudah tahu lah macam mana, dia akan sumbat peti-peti undi itu dengan dia punya, apa nama, voting slip. Tetapi kalau kita dapat kemenangan sampai sepuluh ribu, dua puluh ribu, dia tak kemungkinan nak sumbat peti undi dengan apa nama, dengan kertas mengundi yang ada kepadanya.
Sebab itu, saya harap semua macam ini juga, penuh semangat, pagi-pagi pergi undi. Jangan tunggu sampai petang, kita dah tahu hujan. Jadi pergi undi Pakatan Harapan, jangan sekali-kali undi kati ataupun apa nama, bulan, bulan itu tak nampak dah, warna pun dah hilang. Saya tahu di sini pun ada orang PAS ramai. Mat Sabu tahulah dia main dulu. Dia dah jumpa dengan orang itu. Tapi, dulu dia dengar nasihat Mat Sabu, saya cadang dia patut dengar sekali lagi nasihat Mat Sabu. Mat Sabu kata Tok saya tak undi PAS lagi kerana PAS jual diri kepada UMNO.
Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan inilah peluang terakhir bagi kita. Kalaulah Najib menang, dia akan teruskan dengan dasar-dasar dan penekatannya. Di antaranya ialah nak curi duit lagi. Duit siapa yang dia nak curi? Kita lah. Dia ambil duit kerajaan, kita bayar cukai, itu duit kita. Kalau dia pinjam pun, kita yang kena bayar. Dia curi duit itu, dia pinjam, kita yang kena bayar juga. Sebab itu, dia adalah pencuri besar. Seluruh dunia panggil dia pencuri tetapi bila berkatakan Najib, tak malukah berjumpa dengan Presiden Indonesia yang tahu kamu pencuri? Dia tak ada apa, duduk senyum macam itu lah. Orang letakannya duduk di tepi sekali sebelah Aung San Suu Kyi. Aung San pun tak berapa suci. Itulah tempat Najib ini.
Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan, Najib tak tahu malu. Dia boleh menghadap dengan orang yang tahu dia curi, dia buat macam nak bagi nasihat kepada orang pula, buat syarahan. Buat syarahan kepada pemimpin-pemimpin negara seolah-olah dia boleh nasihat orang. Yang tahu nasihat ialah macam mana mencuri, itulah nasihat Najib. Dia belajar daripada kawan dia, Jho Low. Jho Low ini, tak mahu balik dah. Balik masuk jail lah, dia duduk di mana tak tahu. Yang tahu dia duduk atas kapal, tak berani turun, duduk atas kapal, kapal itu dirampas. Dia dirampas oleh polis Indonesia bersama dengan MBI America. Bila dia dirampas saja maka kita sini dapat tahu bahawa Jho Low yang menjadi pemilik kapal ini. Semua orang tahu, seluruh dunia tahu. Kalau dia tidak curi, takkan orang nak rampas. Tetapi kita berasa sedih ada pegawai tinggi di negara ini iaitu Ketua Polis Negara, KPN, kata, “Tidak ada kaitan antara Jho Low dengan 1MDB.” Apalah nak nafi, semua orang tahu, awak tahu bahawa yang benar ialah Jho Low curi duit 1MDB. Kalau kita menang pun, kita nak kena perah Jho Low ini keluar balik duit dia. Lepas perah itu masuk dalam tetapi sebelum masuk dalam kita perah dulu. (Applause)
Inilah Jho Low, sahabat karib Najib dan Rosmah. Ada wanita cantik di Australia bagi cincin berlian, orang itu bagi balik lah. Dia tak mahu lah. Ini cara Jho Low berkawan dengan ratu-ratu cantik. Bagi duit, bagi apa nama, diamond dan macam-macam lagi. Tetapi yang dia bagi yang banyak sekali ialah kepada Rosmah. Rosmah dapat cincin berlian berwarna merah jambu, bukan main harga dia bermillion-million ringgit. Sebab itu saya dah tahu lah, dengan nama Najib, kalau tidak Rosmah alih tengok Jho Low pula. Saya tengok gambar Jho Low ini bukanlah segak sangat. Yang segak duitnya. Ada orang yang cantik-cantik pun berkawan dengan dia pasal duit. Saya fikir Anwar—apa nama, Rosmah pun macam itu juga nak derma berlian dan sebagainya. Inilah orangnya yang menjadi sahabat karib Najib dengan Rosmah.
Seperti yang saya katakan tadi, kita berpeluang untuk nyah pergilah Najib ini. Tak susah, cuma nak pangkah sahaja. Tengok kita dah tunjuk macam mana nak pangkah. Ini, pangkah simbol Parti Keadilan Rakyat ini. Inilah simbol parti kita. (Applause) Sama ada parti DAP ataupun KEADILAN ataupun AMANAH ataupun parti yang diharamkan, kita pakai ini satu sahaja. Bermakna bahawa kita sudah kalau tidak diserahdaftar disatukan tetapi cari daripada semangat kita, kita sudah disatukan. Jadi itulah sebabnya yang bila kita berkempen, kita berkempen bersama. Ada AMANAH, ada KEADILAN, ada Parti Pribumi pun yang tidak ada di sini parti DAP, parti DAP tidak ramai di Langkawi ini tetapi Orang Cina sokong Pakatan Harapan. Ini dinyatakan oleh mereka.
Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan saya ucapkan terima kasih kepada tuan-tuan dan puan-puan yang sudi hadir pada malam ini. Alhamdulillah tidak ada hujan. Semalam ingat hujan lebat tetapi malam ini tidak ada hujan, kita boleh berkumpul dalam keadaan yang selesa saya yakin ini adalah satu petanda yang baik kerana kita akan dapat cantumkan diri kita dalam Pakatan ini dan kita beri kemenangan kepada Pakatan Harapan. Inshallah kita akan dapat banyak nikmat daripada Kerajaan Pakatan Harapan kerana kerajaan Pakatan Harapan bukanlah seperti Najib. Kita bukan akan dipimpin oleh apa nama, seorang penyagak, penyamun, lanun, pencuri, kawak, semua ini.
Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan, pada malam ini saya diberi tugas untuk menzahirkan ataupun menyiarkan nama-nama calon-calon Parti Pribumi di negeri Kedah. (Applause) Ialah kita seronok, tentulah ada orang yang tak dapat. Yang bercita-cita dia akan dapat tetapi dia tak dapat, tetapi dalam perjuangan tak bolehlah semua menang. Kalau nak perdana menteri, satu sahaja. Kalau semua nak menjadi perdana menteri, rosak lah negara, jadi perang. Jadi ini adalah nama-nama calon yang telah diputuskan oleh kita bagi negeri Kedah, tetapi terhad kepada calon-calon Parti Pribumi sahaja.
Jadi inilah namanya. Untuk Dewan Undangan Negeri, untuk Ayer Hitam, Datuk A. Aziz bin Mohamad, dia tidak di sini sekarang. Bukit Kayu Hitam, Halimaton Shaadiah binti Saad. Jitra, Yang Berhormat Dato Seri Haji Mukhriz Tun Mahathir. Anak Bukit, Yang Berhormat Datuk IR Amiruddin bin Hamzah. Bukit Lada, Muhammad Aizad Roslan. Kuala Nerang, Syed Fazil bin Said. Sungai Tiang, Abdul Razak bin Khamis. Jeneri, Muhammad Nazari bin Abu Hassan. Bayu, ini bukan bayu yang ada di sini ini yang naik motosikal pakai baju hitam, ini bayu tempat dekat dengan Baling saya ingat. Abdul Rahim bin Haji Kecik. Guar Chempedak, Mohamad Safuan bin Sabari. Tanjung Dawar, Mejar (Bersara) Anuar bin Abdul Hamid. Bandar Baharu, Dato Azimi bin Daim. Kuah, Muhammad Firdaus bin Ahmad. Kita nak orang muda sama ada tetapi lama-lama dia tua. Macam saya dulu pun, masuk masih muda, tapi ini dahlah tua. Ayer Hangat, Johari bin Bular, siapa tak besa tengok dia?
Sekarang ini, bagi parlimen pula. Jerlun, Yang Berhormat Dato Seri Haji Mukhriz Tun Mahathir. Kubang Pasu, Yang Berhormat Datuk IR Amiruddin bin Hamzah. Dia pun dua jawatan, dua calon, dua tempat iaitu satu Anak Bukit, satu di Kubang Pasu. Mukhriz pun satu di Jerlun parlimen, satu lagi di Jitra. Jadi kita tidak tahu lah apa yang dia nak jadi. Pendang, Wan Saiful bin Wan Jan. Baling, Mohamad Taufik bin Haji Yaacob. Jerai, Akhramsyah Muammar Ubaidah bin Sanusi. Itu saja lah.",somewhat populist
gpd_Malaysia_Mohamad_Famous_1,Malaysia_Mohamad_Famous_1.txt,speeches_20251120/Malaysia_Mohamad_Famous_1.txt,Malaysia,Mahathir Mohamad,1,Famous,2018,East Asia & Pacific,2,0.44999999999999996,0.44999999,3318,6978,"Ucapan dasar Pengerusi BERSATU, Tun Dr Mahathir Mohamad pada Perhimpunan Agung Tahunan Kali Kedua BERSATU

1. Bersyukurlah kita kerana dapat bersama-sama mengadakan Perhimpunan Agung Tahunan Kali ke-2 bagi parti kita, Parti Pribumi Bersatu Malaysia di Pusat Konvensyen Antarabangsa Putrajaya (PICC) ini. Berada di PICC ini pun adalah satu kejayaan. Dahulu kita tidak pun dapat berdekatan di sini. Alhamdulillah.
2. Kesyukuran ini juga kerana kita dapat mengadakan perhimpunan ini dengan penuh rasa tenang dan atas kesedaran bahawa kita telah berjaya mencapai sebahagian besar dari perjuangan PPBM.
3. Jika pada perhimpunan yang pertama kita hanyalah sebuah parti pembangkang yang dianggap tidak berkeupayaan menandingi gabungan parti pemerintah, kita berhimpun pada kali ini sebagai satu anggota gabungan yang memerintah.
4. Kerana itu kita perlu bersyukur. Walaupun kita yakin kemenangan itu datang dari kerja kuat ahli-ahli parti dan rakan-rakan dari komponen Pakatan Harapan, semestinya kita menyedari bahawa ianya ditentukan oleh Allah SWT jua. Kita berdoa kepada Allah meminta sesuatu bagi kita. Tetapi jangan kita lupa Allah tidak akan makbulkan permintaan jika kita tidak berusaha sendiri ke arahnya.
5. Kejayaan ini tidak harus menjadikan kita bongkak. Sifat bongkak itu amat dibenci Allah SWT. Selain dari itu ia juga tidak disukai oleh masyarakat. Apabila kita bongkak dan sudah tidak disukai oleh masyarakat, kemenangan kita tidak akan berulang.
6. Kemenangan bukan untuk kita gembira sahaja. Ia datang dengan satu tanggungjawab yang berat. Tanggungjawab yang perlu kita tunaikan ialah memenuhi janji kita semasa berkempen, dan juga yang dibuat dalam manifesto Pakatan Harapan.
7. Semasa kita berkempen kita tidak tahu dengan mendalam akan keadaan kerosakan yang telah menimpa negara. Hanya setelah kita mengambil-alih Kerajaan, barulah kita tahu kerosakan yang berlaku amatlah teruk dan merangkumi hampir setiap bahagian pentadbiran Kerajaan. Walaupun sudah tujuh bulan sejak kita mengambil alih tampuk Kerajaan, kita masih menemui kerosakan dalam jentera Kerajaan dan kewangan negara yang tersembunyi dahulu.
8. Malangnya, rakyat sudah bosan dan tidak lagi memberi perhatian kepada kesalahan Kerajaan terdahulu. Mereka hanya ingin lihat hasil pemulihan negara oleh kita. Ramai rakyat yang tidak pun memberi perhatian kepada tindakan undang-undang yang diambil terhadap pemimpin dahulu. Sebaliknya dengan lantang pemimpin dahulu cuba mengajar kita tentang cara-cara kita tangani masalah. Masalah yang ditinggal oleh mereka. Jika mereka begitu pandai, kenapakah mereka tidak betulkan kerosakan semasa mereka memerintah dahulu.
9. Di dalam negara, Peguam Negara telah memulakan langkah-langkah awal untuk mendakwa pemimpin-pemimpin terdahulu atas kesalahan salah-guna kuasa dan rasuah oleh mereka. Tindakan yang diambil ke atas mereka bukan disebabkan oleh perasaan ingin balas dendam oleh kita, tetapi hanya kerana menghormati pemerintahan mengikut undang-undang, the rule of law.
10. Amatlah mengecewakan apabila ada yang menolak kesalahan yang jelas telah dilakukan oleh pemimpin-pemimpin yang terdahulu. Jika kesalahan mereka tidak diproses mengikut undang-undang maka kita akan dituduh melepas geram dan membalas dendam. Tetapi proses undang-undang mengambil masa. Untuk dilihat kita memerintah mengikut undang-undang kita perlu terima kelewatan proses.
11. Sudah tentu percubaan pemimpin-pemimpin dahulu untuk sekarang menjadi juara orang Melayu dengan mengambil bahagian dalam demonstrasi baru-baru ini tidak ikhlas. Rakyat tidak akan tertipu dengan perbuatan ini. Jika mereka ikhlas, masalah yang kita hadapi tidak akan berlaku.
12. Apa yang sebenar berlaku ialah parti yang dahulu disanjung tinggi kerana perjuangan melawan Malayan Union dan memerdekakan negara, sudah ditolak oleh rakyat, khususnya orang Melayu, kerana terlibat dengan rasuah, pencurian dan pengamalan pemerintahan kleptokrasi. Hari ini mereka hancur berkecai kerana perbuatan mereka sendiri.
13. Hari ini yang penting ialah pemerintahan negara yang baik oleh kita - kita dalam Parti BERSATU bersama rakan kita dalam Pakatan Harapan. Setakat ini kita berjaya menubuh kerajaan di peringkat Pusat dan di beberapa buah negeri. Tidak ada rusuhan berlaku. Pemerintahan kita membawa ketenangan dan kestabilan yang menjayakan rakyat dan pelabur. Ekonomi negara sekarang tumbuh dengan baik walaupun dunia tidak stabil.
14. Hutang kita sedang ditangani dengan baik dan jentera pentadbiran pun dibersih dan dipulih semula. Malangnya rakyat, terutama golongan miskin merasai tekanan kos sara hidup yang tinggi.
15. Kerajaan dahulu pernah memberi duit percuma kepada rakyat secara rambang. Kita Pakatan Harapan (PH) tidak mampu. Sebabnya kita tidak mampu ialah kerana kita tidak selewengkan wang kerajaan. Lagipun sebahagian yang tidak kecil dari pendapatan kerajaan terpaksa diguna untuk bayar hutang dan faedah yang amat tinggi. Jika hutang tidak dibayar maka kita boleh menjadi muflis – bankrap. Kalau jadi muflis, semua pendapatan kita akan diguna untuk bayar hutang. Tidak akan ada wang sedikit pun untuk bantu rakyat. Inilah malapetaka yang dibawa oleh kerajaan dahulu.
16. Kita sedang usaha menurunkan harga barang. Tetapi ini akan mengambil masa sedikit. Insya-Allah kos sara hidup akan turun.
17. Parti Pribumi Bersatu Malaysia adalah parti Melayu/Bumiputera seluruh Malaysia. Ia ditubuh kerana UMNO, parti Melayu sudah tidak lagi mengutamakan perjuangan asal parti itu – iaitu melindungi dan memajukan orang Melayu dan Bumiputera.
18. UMNO ditubuh kerana orang Melayu sangsi akan kemampuan mereka bersaing dengan kaum lain di Malaysia, terutama apabila merdeka. Di zaman British mereka sudah pun ketinggalan, miskin dan lemah. Hanya dengan bersatu dalam parti politik baharulah mereka dapat yakinkan diri mereka bahawa hak mereka sebagai anak watan tidak akan terlucut dan mereka akan terpinggir di negara mereka sendiri. Penubuhan UMNO meyakinkan mereka bahawa kuasa politik Melayu/Bumiputera boleh menjaminkan keselamatan mereka.
19. Selama 50 tahun lebih setelah merdeka kedudukan mereka terpelihara walaupun kuasa mereka semakin lemah kerana perpecahan di kalangan mereka.
20. Kemudian kepimpinan yang mengambil alih pada 2003 menukar haluan. Dari sebuah parti yang menjadi juara orang Melayu dan Bumiputera, UMNO diubah menjadi alat untuk perkaya diri pemimpin. Rasuah oleh pemimpin berkembang dengan pesat sehingga melibat bukan sahaja pemimpin politik tetapi sebahagian dari anggota kerajaan. Kepimpinan kerajaan sendiri menjadi pengamal utama rasuah dalam negara. Dengan itu pengamalan rasuah berkembang di kalangan pemimpin politik dan juga pentadbiran.
21. Rakyat menderita kerana harga barangan dan khidmat yang tinggi. Khidmat dari anggota kerajaan juga tinggi kerana rasuah. Peniaga dibelasah dengan lebih teruk lagi, dipaksa membayar cukai yang tidak mengikut undang-undang.
22. Cogankata negara dialih kepada “Cash is King”. Duit itu Raja. Maka seluruh anggota kerajaan, politik dan pentadbiran mengejar wang tanpa mengambil kira halal atau haram.
23. Semua ini merosakkan negara terutamanya kewangannya. Daripada sebuah parti yang demokratik, UMNO sudah jadi suatu dictatorship yang tugas utamanya ialah mengekal pemimpin tertingginya. Wang yang dicuri ditabur untuk mendapat sokongan rakyat. Dan rasuah pun merebak luas.
24. Pemimpin UMNO yang tidak senang dengan apa yang sudah berlaku kepada parti cuba membawa balik parti ke landasan asal, tetapi gagal. Nasihat ditolak oleh pucuk kepimpinan. Khidmat kepada negara dan rakyat tidak dianggap boleh menawan hati rakyat. Yang diperlukan ialah sogokan wang. Jika duit tidak cukup, duit dipinjam atas nama kerajaan, tetapi duit itu dicuri untuk sogok rakyat.
25. Maka pemimpin UMNO yang sedar akan pertukaran matlamat dan dasar yang berlaku memilih untuk keluar dari UMNO dan menubuh parti lain. Jika parti baru ini berhasrat mendapat sokongan orang Melayu, maka ia hendaklah menjadi parti Melayu/Bumiputera. Ternampak jelas parti campuran kaum belum dapat diterima oleh orang Melayu. Sebaliknya tanpa sokongan pengundi Melayu, tidak mungkin mana-mana parti kalahkan UMNO.
26. Dengan itu maka ditubuhlah parti kita, Parti Pribumi Bersatu Malaysia. Parti ini adalah parti Melayu Bumiputera dari segi keahliannya. Tetapi itu sahaja persamaan dengan UMNO selepas 2003. Kita tidak ingin menjadikan UMNO selepas 2003 sebagai contoh bagi kita. Sebaliknya, Parti Pribumi dengan ikhlas berjuang untuk Pribumi. Soalnya kenapakah keutamaan diberi kepada pribumi dalam negara berbilang kaum. Tentulah PPBM ini menjadi parti perkauman.
27. Kita sudah merdeka lebih dari 60 tahun. Di waktu kita mencapai kemerdekaan harapan kita ialah Malaysia akan menjadi negara satu bangsa yang bertutur kata dalam satu bahasa, berbudaya yang sama. Tetapi harapan ini tidak menjadi kenyataan. Masing-masing kaum tegas untuk kekalkan identiti kaum mereka. Dengan ini kewujudan satu bangsa terhalang, tidak tercapai. Ini tidak berlaku di negara-negara berbilang bangsa yang lain, umpamanya Amerika Syarikat, Australia, Indonesia dan Thailand.
28. Pengasingan identiti ini tidak mengapa jika tidak terdapat pengasingan dalam aktiviti hidup dan kemajuan. Rata-rata kita dapati pengasingan kawasan juga iaitu kaum-kaum tidak tinggal bersama, tetapi di kawasan masing-masing. Ini pula mengasingkan aktiviti hidup yang berlainan. Umpama satu kaum ramai di bandar, satu kaum di desa dan satu lagi di ladang-ladang. Perpisahan ini mempunyai kesan kepada kemajuan ekonomi dan agihan kekayaan antara mereka. Umumnya yang tinggal di bandar lebih maju dan kaya dari yang tinggal di desa.
29. Oleh kerana orang Melayu dan Bumiputera lain bermastautin di desa maka mereka kurang maju berbanding dengan kaum di bandar.
30. Sekarang ini pula bandar sedang berkembang dengan luasnya. Kerana kemiskinan penduduk Bumiputera di pinggir bandar sering menjual tanah mereka dan berpindah jauh dari bandar, iaitu ke kawasan yang kurang peluang untuk menjana kekayaan. Maka jarak perpisahan antara yang tinggal di bandar dan di luar bandar pun menjadi lebih jauh.
31. Semua yang berlaku ini menakutkan orang Melayu di luar bandar dan orang Melayu dalam bandar yang lebih prihatin terhadap nasib masa depan mereka. Mereka mencari perlindungan dari nasib yang buruk yang akan menimpa mereka, bahkan sudah pun menimpa mereka.
32. Sebenarnya keselamatan mereka hanya dapat ditentukan oleh mereka sendiri dengan meningkatkan keupayaan mereka. Dengan perkataan lain mereka hendaklah kejar ilmu dan kecekapan dan sanggup bertekun dalam usaha menjayakan diri mereka. Tetapi mereka sudah begitu jauh ketinggalan di belakang sehingga sukar bagi mereka mengejar kaum yang kaya. Mereka berpendapat mereka perlu dilindungi dan untuk ini, pada pendapat mereka hanya boleh dilakukan oleh kaum mereka sendiri melalui politik. Sebab itulah parti yang disertai dan dipimpin oleh mereka sendiri perlu diadakan.
33. Inilah sebab-sebabnya kita tubuh Parti Pribumi Bersatu sebagai parti Melayu dan Bumiputera. Sementara kita lindungi Melayu/Bumiputera, caranya bukanlah dengan merampas hak dan harta orang lain. Tidak pernah sepanjang kita merdeka ada rampasan dibuat.
34. Buat beberapa abad negara telah perkenal Dasar Ekonomi Baru; dasar yang bertujuan mengurangkan jarak perpisahan antara kaum. Dasar ini telah menambah sedikit kejayaan dan kemajuan Bumiputera. Tetapi oleh kerana pesaing mereka melonjak lebih jauh dan pantas, maka jarak perpisahan juga menjadi terlalu luas untuk mereka sendiri melintasi.
35. Kita orang Melayu dan juga Bumiputera lain mesti pegang kepada kebenaran. Meletak kesalahan kepada orang lain memang sedap tetapi mereka tidak akan betulkan diri mereka untuk menyelesaikan masalah kita. Sebaliknya jika kita akui bahawa ada juga kesalahan pada diri kita, maka bagi yang ikhlas dan jujur, pembetulan boleh dibuat oleh kita. Kita berkuasa ke atas diri kita, tidak ke atas orang lain.
36. Saya, tidak ingin sebut di sini apakah kesalahan kita. Tetapi kita perlu akui bahawa banyak sudah tindakan yang dibuat untuk memperbaiki prestasi kita oleh kerajaan tetapi kejayaan amatlah menyedihkan.
37. Sebabnya ialah sambutan oleh kita tidak seperti dirancang dan diharapkan. Kerajaan boleh adakan dasar dan layanan kepada kita tetapi jika sambutan oleh kita masih seperti dahulu, hasilnya akan menjadi sama dan mengecewakan.
38. Dalam percubaan Dasar Ekonomi Baru kita dapati kaum wanita lebih serius dan berjaya dari kaum lelaki. Di mana-mana sahaja kita dapati kejayaan yang tinggi didapati oleh kaum wanita. Ada di antara yang sudah jadi jutawan pun hanya dengan membuat keropok lekor, tudung kepala dan alat kecantikan wanita. Mereka juga mengeluarkan makanan biasa yang tahan lama dan dibungkus dengan cukup menarik. Ternampak jelas jika diberi peluang kaum wanita mampu berjaya lagi.
39. Oleh itu kita akan tambah punca modal, peluang, lesen dan kontrak juga kepada kaum wanita termasuk di kampung. Kita akan perkenal jenis perniagaan dan peluang baru kepada mereka.
40. Untuk meningkatkan kebolehan mereka, latihan dan pelajaran bagi mereka akan ditambah. Keutamaan akan diberi kepada catitan urusan perniagaan. Amanah Ikhtiar Malaysia (AIM) akan diperbesarkan dan contoh-contoh yang baik dalam perniagaan wanita akan dibantu lagi untuk membesar perniagaan mereka. Mereka yang berjaya akan dibantu lagi. Pertandingan antara mereka akan diadakan dan hadiah akan diberi kepada yang berjaya besar.
41. Berkenaan dengan peluang bekerja dalam kerajaan dan swasta, yang menjadi ukuran ialah kelulusan yang baik dan pengalaman yang luas. Diskriminasi terhadap wanita semata-mata kerana jenis mereka akan dihapuskan.
42. Generasi muda juga akan diberi layanan istimewa, Dalam pertanian dan perniagaan kita kerap mencuba menjayakan mereka yang sudah ada dalam bidang-bidang ini. Hakikatnya ialah yang sudah dewasa sukar untuk menerima cara-cara dan teknologi baru. Sebaliknya yang muda lebih mudah dibentuk dan disemai dengan cara-cara baru. Kita lihat umpamanya penggunaan komputer dan telefon bimbit lebih mudah dikuasai oleh generasi muda berbanding dengan generasi tua.
43. Ramai dari generasi muda lebih terlatih dan berpelajaran. Pengalaman mereka mungkin kurang. Tetapi ini boleh diatasi dengan pendedahan kepada kerja sebagai pekerja upahan.
44. Hari ini terdapat contoh-contoh yang baik dikalangan orang muda dalam bidang industri, pertanian moden dan ternakan.
45. Negara kita amat bergantung kepada barangan dan makanan yang diimport dari negara asing. Sebaliknya barangan ini boleh dikeluarkan dalam negara kita.
46. Generasi muda akan diberi latihan dan peluang untuk memasuki bidang-bidang ini. Bermula dengan bekerja sebagai tenaga upahan, yang berminat boleh diberi peluang dan dibantu untuk memasuki bidang yang hampir sama, sebagai entrepreneur.
47. Saya tumpukan kepada apa yang akan dilakukan oleh pemimpin politik dari PPBM dalam Kerajaan Pakatan Harapan kerana masa berpolitik sudah berakhir. Kita sekarang menjadi sebahagian dari Kerajaan yang memerintah. Dan Kerajaan yang memerintah berkuasa untuk melayani keperluan rakyat. Kuasa sebagai pemimpin dalam Kerajaan bukan untuk dibanggakan. Ia juga bukan untuk mendapat keuntungan bagi diri sendiri. Kuasa pemimpin Kerajaan ialah untuk memaju dan membangun negara. Dari ini rakyat akan hidup lebih selesa dan sempurna.
48. Matlamat kita masih sama. Kita ingin jadikan negara ini negara maju setaraf dengan negara maju yang lain. Negara maju tidak bermakna jika kita, sebagai sebahagian dari rakyat negara, terus tidak maju seperti kemajuan yang dicapai oleh rakyat lain. Kita tidak hendak jadi puak yang miskin di negara yang kaya. Nikmat dalam negara ini hendaklah dikecapi bersama oleh semua kaum.
49. Ada di antara kita yang berpendapat bahawa kemajuan boleh dicapai jika dihentikan bantuan oleh pemerintah. Yang anehnya ialah orang yang mempunyai pendapat sedemikian mendapat kemajuan kerana dibantu oleh kerajaan, diberi peluang dan tempat dalam kerajaan.
50. Bagi yang lemah, tongkat boleh membantu. Bantuan seperti ini tidak harus dikekalkan. Apabila sahaja kekuatan kembali tongkat perlu digugur.
51. Pendapat bahawa tongkat adalah tanda kemuliaan adalah salah. Mengekalkan tongkat kerana kemuliaan bagi diri tidak berasas. Sebaliknya yang berdiri tegak dalam menghadapi serta mengatasi cabaran – mereka inilah orang yang mulia.
52. Kita jangan tipu diri. Memanggil diri kita Tuan tidak menjadikan kita Tuan jika kita masih menjadi kuli orang.
Saudara, saudari sekalian,
53. Hari ini orang Melayu berada dalam keadaan yang tidak menentu dan kehilangan haluan. Parti mereka kalah dan berpecah sehingga secara berkesan tidak wujud lagi. Pemimpin mereka bertelagah dan ahli tidak tahu apa yang sudah jadi pada mereka. Ada yang keluar dari UMNO, ada cuba hidupkan UMNO. Ada yang masih fikir mereka sebagai sebuah parti politik boleh bergabung dengan parti-parti lain, mendapat cukup bilang untuk mendiri kerajaan campuran. Ada pemimpin yang percaya mereka akan pimpin kerajaan campuran baru ini.
54. Semua harapan ini meleset, mimpi Mat Jenin, mimpi akan sesuatu yang tidak berasas dan tidak akan berlaku.
55. UMNO sudah hancur, dihancur oleh pemimpin yang tamak dan anggap manusia boleh dibeli dengan duit. Sebuah parti yang mulia, dibangun untuk menyelamatkan kaum bangsa Melayu, sekarang dikalah, dihina dan tidak terdaya dipulih semula.
56. Malangnya yang sebenar menjadi mangsa ialah orang Melayu, penduduk pribumi di negara bertuah ini. Mereka sudah hilang jaguh mereka.
57. Apakah Parti Pribumi Bersatu Malaysia yang ditubuh untuk menyelamatkan orang Melayu dan Bumiputera lain harus berdiam diri dan membiar kehancuran Melayu/Bumiputera berterusan. Walaupun kita bukan pewaris UMNO tetapi kita bertanggungjawab kepada orang Melayu dan Bumiputera.
58. Rasis, perkaumankah ini? Dalam negara satu etnik pun apabila berlaku perpisahan yang terlalu jauh antara yang miskin dan yang kaya, sejarah melapor bahawa rusuhan berlaku, perang saudara akan tercetus dan negara akan hancur.
59. Apatah lagi jika perpisahan antara miskin dan kaya ditambah dengan perpisahan antara kaum, yang miskin dari satu kaum, yang kaya dari kaum lain.
60. Kombinasi antara dua faktor ini amatlah merbahaya. Ia boleh mencetuskan rusuhan yang serius dan mendalam. Rusuhan akan membawa malapetaka kepada semua rakyat Malaysia. Tidak semestinya rusuhan akan berlaku. Tetapi ralatkah kita ketepikan kemungkinan.
61. Kaum tidak dapat ditukar. Tetapi jarak antara miskin dan kaya boleh dikurangkan jika tidak pun dihapuskan.
62. Tidak bertanggungjawablah kita jika kita tidak cuba elak dari rusuhan kaum dengan sekurang-kurangnya mengurangkan jarak antara miskin dan kaya.
63. Melayu sekarang sudah keliru, kehilangan pemimpin, kehilangan haluan. UMNO sudah tidak ada lagi. Siapa, parti yang mana yang boleh mereka bergantung?
64. Jikalau tidak BERSATU, parti mana? Mungkinkah PAS? Saya tak nak komen. Pilihlah PAS. Itu bukan pilihan saya.
65. Ya, orang UMNO memang bersalah. Tak payah saya cerita lagi. Kita semua tahu. Tetapi apakah kerana UMNO bersalah kita harus salahkan seluruh bangsa Melayu?
66. Ramai yang tidak senang melihat penerimaan bekas ahli UMNO oleh BERSATU. Mereka takut bekas-bekas ini akan membawa masuk budaya UMNO.
67. Kita BERSATU tidak mudah terima. Ada syarat. Mesti keluar dari UMNO dan jadi bebas. Sebagai bebas secara ikhlas sokong Pakatan Harapan dan BERSATU. Tidak akan ada penerimaan oleh BERSATU sebagai satu kumpulan bekas UMNO. Hanya akan diterima sebagai individu bebas. Rekod akan dikaji dengan teliti.
68. Jika diterima, tidak boleh pegang jawatan sehingga PRU-15. Lama. Ya lama. Ujian keikhlasan tidak boleh dipercepat. Hanya jika betul-betul ikhlas, jika sudah buang budaya UMNO, barulah boleh diterima sesuai untuk pegang jawatan.
69. Kita akan tentukan mereka tidak diberi peluang mengembang fahaman dan cara-cara mereka, iaitu cara UMNO. BERSATU bersih dan kita akan tentukan ia terus bersih. Yang akan bertukar ialah bekas parti lain. Mereka akan serap budaya kita. Mereka akan bekerjasama dengan kita.
70. Dengan itu kita akan jadi pelindung kepada orang Melayu dan Bumiputera – pelindung sementara – kerana pelindung yang sebenar ialah kita sendiri.
71. Lindungan bagi kita akan terhasil jika kita tidak miskin. Selagi kita miskin kita tidak akan berasa selamat. Bukan politik, bukan kuasa politik, bukan parti politik yang boleh melindungi kita. Kita sudah lihat bagaimana parti politik kita yang terkenal kekuatannya, tetapi parti politik inilah yang meletak kita dalam keadaan amat bahaya.
72. Tetapi jika kita kaya, jika kita berjaya dalam semua bidang, tidak ada siapa yang boleh ancam kita.
73. Tetapi bagaimanakah kita boleh berjaya, boleh jadi kaya dan maju. Sebenarnya kita ada kebolehan. Tetapi kebolehan yang tidak diguna oleh kita, tidak akan menjayakan kita.
74. BERSATU tahu bagaimana kita boleh berjaya, bagaimana kita boleh selamatkan diri kita, orang Melayu dan Bumiputera lain.
75. Tak perlu saya ulas di sini bagaimana BERSATU boleh ubah nasib orang Melayu/Bumiputera. Yang kita minta hanyalah kepercayaan dan kesanggupan menurut cara yang akan diperkenal oleh kita.
76. Percayalah, Melayu boleh selamatkan diri mereka sendiri. Percayalah hanya Melayu sahaja yang boleh selamatkan diri sendiri.
Tuan-tuan dan puan-puan,
77. Kita bersidang bukan kerana perlembagaan kita suruh kita bersidang: bukan kerana takut ROS. Kita bersidang kerana kita berhasrat menyelamatkan orang Melayu. Kita bersidang kerana kita ingin majukan orang Melayu.
78. Kita bersidang kerana kita berhasrat memulihkan maruah bangsa kita.
79. Inilah tujuan kita berpolitik. Bukan kerana nak jadi Perdana Menteri, atau Menteri, atau Menteri Besar dan Ketua Menteri.
80. Kita berpolitik supaya kita tidak lagi akan bergantung kepada politik. Kita berpolitik untuk menyelamat dan membebaskan kita melalui kejayaan sebagai satu bangsa yang mampu bersaing dengan siapa sahaja, tiap seorang dari kita berdaya tahan sendiri tanpa bertongkat.
81. Untuk perjuangan yang mulia ini, berkorbanlah apa sahaja. Hasil pengorbanan kita akan dihargai oleh anak cucu kita. Akan berkatalah mereka, jika tidak kerana pengorbanan oleh kita, maka akan tertinggallah mereka di pinggir hutan, miskin papa di tanah air mereka.
82. Ya. Saya akan dituduh rasis kerana pendedahan nasib Melayu/Bumiputera ini. Tetapi selama lebih 70 tahun saya telah lihat kemerosotan yang berlaku pada kaum bangsa saya.
83. Tak mengapalah jika diburukkan nama saya asalkan bangsa saya sedar akan nasib buruk yang akan menimpa mereka di masa hadapan. Sedarlah bahawa kita yang salah. Tak usah cari kesalahan orang lain. Pemulihan berada di tangan kita. Usaha yang diperlukan tidak sebegitu besar. Insya-Allah akan terhasillah pengorbanan kita yang sedikit.
84. Itulah pesanan saya. Peluang bagi menyampaikan ucapan seperti ini di tahun hadapan mungkin ada, mungkin tidak. Justeru, peluang ini tidak boleh dilepaskan. Diharap bangsaku akan tolak budaya lama dan cipta budaya baru, budaya yang tetap akan menyelamatkan kita.
85. Maka dengan ini saya rasmikan mesyuarat Perhimpunan Agung Tahunan Kali Kedua BERSATU.
Sekian.
Wabillahitaufik walhidayah, wassallamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuh.",not populist
gpd_Malaysia_Mohamad_International_1,Malaysia_Mohamad_International_1.txt,speeches_20251120/Malaysia_Mohamad_International_1.txt,Malaysia,Mahathir Mohamad,1,International,2018,East Asia & Pacific,2,0.6,0.60000002,2954,3465,"The following is the full text of Prime Minister Tun Dr Mahathir Mohamad’s speech during the General Debate of the 74th session of the United Nations General Assembly in New York on Sept 27 2019
INTRODUCTION - VETO POWER
1. I would like to join others in congratulating you Mr. President on your election as the President of the 74th Session of the United Nations General Assembly. I would also like to thank Her Excellency Maria Espinosa, for her dedication and stewardship in successfully completing the work of the 73rd Session of the General Assembly.
2. Malaysia welcomes the theme of this year’s General Assembly, which is, “Galvanising multilateral efforts for poverty eradication, quality education, climate action and inclusion”. The key message of this theme is “galvanising multilateral efforts”, which is what the United Nations (UN) stands for. I will propose a few.
3. Almost three quarters of a century ago five countries claimed victory in the Second World War. On the basis of that victory they insisted on the right practically to rule the world. And so, they gave themselves veto powers over the rest of the world in the organisation they built – an organisation they claim would end wars in the solution of conflicts.
4. The veto power - they must know was against all the principles of human rights which they themselves claim to be the champions. It killed the very purpose of the great organisation that they had created. It ensured that all solution to all conflicts could be negated by any one of them. Broken up into ideological factions they frustrated all attempts at solving problems.
5. Each one of them can negate the wishes of the nearly 200 other members. It is totally and absolutely undemocratic. Yet, there are among them those who berate other countries of the world for not being democratic or being not democratic enough.
6. How much longer should this group be allowed to exercise this power? How long, forever? The unspoken time frame seems to be eternal.
7. That very power has resulted in an arms race. Each one of the five rely on their military might in order to challenge any attempt to take their power away. They feel they must be well armed to retain their right to be the privileged five.
8. It is this structure of the United Nations that renders it incapable of achieving its principle objectives - that of preventing wars between nations. Indeed, the structure had enabled the promotion of war within countries and between countries.
9. True, the war-like European countries have not gone to war with each other over the past two-thirds of a century. But elsewhere there is evidence that European countries have caused wars to break out, arms and funds to be supplied and active participation in prolonging the wars. It is apparently good for business, for weapons sale.
ISRAEL - THE ORIGIN OF TERRORISM
10. The first act engineered by the Western countries is the creation of the state of Israel by seizing Palestinian land and expelling its 90% Arab population. Since then wars have been fought in many countries, many related to the creation of Israel. And now we have terrorism when there was none before or at least none on the present scale. Military action against Acts of terrorism will not succeed. We need to identify the cause and remove it. But the great powers refuse to deal with the root cause.
11. They prefer military action and sanctions. And they will continue to fail to stop terrorism.
12. Malaysia accepts the state of Israel as a fait accompli. But it cannot accept the blatant seizure of Palestine land by Israel for their settlements as well as the occupation of Jerusalem by Israel. The Palestinians cannot even enter the settlements built on their land.
13. Because of the creation of Israel, there is now enmity towards the Muslims and Islam. Muslims are accused of terrorism even if they did nothing. Muslim countries have been destabilised through the campaign for democracy and regime change. Muslims everywhere have been oppressed, expelled from their countries and refused asylum. Thousands have died at sea and in the severe winters. One cannot deny that in the past there were no massive migration. Now the wars and instability due to regime change have forced them to run away from their countries.
14. I will admit that democracy is a better form of Government than dictatorship. But democracy is not the easiest form of Government to operate. This is especially so when the adoption is overnight. Time should be allowed for a gradual change to democracy. Indeed, the very countries which promote democracy became democratic over a period of decades if not centuries. The result of overnight switch to democracy is destabilisation and civil wars, reducing some into Government-less wilderness. And some of course have reverted to authoritarian regimes worse than the one that was displaced. Unable to suffer from wars and violence their people had to migrate.
15. The great democrats talk incessantly about the rule of law. But they are selective. Friends may break any law and get away scot-free. Thus, Israel can break all the international laws and norms of the world and it will continue to be supported and defended. The unfriendly countries can do nothing right. There is no justice in the world.
16. I must again refer to the fate of the Rohingyas in Myanmar. Many colonies of the West, upon independence, expelled non-natives in their countries. But nowhere have they been as brutal as Myanmar. Even natives massacred, brutally killed and raped in full view of the world backgrounded by the burning houses and villages of the victims. They were forced to migrate and now they dare not return to Myanmar even when offered. They cannot trust the Myanmar military unless some form of non-Myanmar protection is given.
17. The helplessness of the world in stopping atrocities inflicted on the Rohingyas in Myanmar had reduced the regard for the resolution of the UN. Now, despite UN resolution on Jammu and Kashmir, the country has been invaded and occupied. There may be reasons for this action but it is still wrong. The problem must be solved by peaceful means. India should work with Pakistan to resolve this problem. Ignoring the UN would lead to other forms of disregard for the UN and the Rule of Law.
18. All the countries of the world wish to prosper, to grow their economies. During their colonial days their wealth had been exploited to enrich their colonial masters. They cannot expect much from their former colonial masters. But they do expect to be allowed to develop their own countries themselves. But they are hampered from doing so.
19. There is much talk about free trade. But all the time new regulations are being introduced which are detrimental to the development of poor countries. This is because proposals on rules and regulations are made by the rich, often secretly. The poor are practically forced to accept them. One example is the Trans Pacific partnership. It was cooked up in Washington with inputs from their big businesses. In the agreement Governments of small countries could be forced to compensate the big foreign companies with huge sums of money, should their decision affect the profitability of the big companies, including future profit.
20. Fortunately, now the powerful country which prepared these agreements has rejected it. With the exclusion of this country, the Agreement has become more palatable. But the agreements still laid down conditions for trade – which negates free trade. We are told that we must remove duties on imports, or reduce it so that foreign products can knock out our infant industries. We are reduced to exporting only raw material. How do we industrialise and create jobs for our people?
21. A classic case of the denial of free trade is the ban on the import of palm oil proposed by the European countries. Unable to sustain the competitiveness of their own edible oils, a campaign is mounted to ban palm oil. It is said that palm oil is poisonous to health, destroys the habitat of longnosed monkeys, reduce carbon dioxide absorption etc. Products of Europe are labelled palm oil free. Biofuel using palm oil are banned.
22. Malaysia produces palm oil. Many poor countries produce palm oil. Malaysia will not clear more forests for palm plantations. We are as concerned about our environment as the Europeans. At the Rio Earth Summit in 1992, Malaysia pledged to maintain at least 50 percent of our land mass under forest cover. We have made good our pledge and better. Our forest cover is currently at 55.3 percent exceeding our Rio pledge.
23. Palm oil is still a big contributor to our economy. There is no evidence that it is poisonous. We appeal to the good sense of the rich not to impoverish us, not to deprive hundreds of thousands of our workers from earning a living. You will be doing a good deed by consuming palm oil.
24. In keeping with the objectives of the United Nations, Malaysia had launched a campaign to criminalise war. It is ridiculous to hang a murderer for killing one person but to glorify the people who are responsible for the deaths of millions of people. Modern wars are total in every way. Not only will combatants be killed but innocent people, the children, the sick and incapacitated are also killed and wounded. Whole countries are devastated, and trillions of dollars lost. In the end, both the victors and losers suffer.
25. We consider ourselves civilised but we are still very primitive since we accept killing people as a way to settle disputes between nations or within nations.
26. There are other ways of settling disputes. We can negotiate or submit to arbitration by third parties. Or we can resort to the courts of law – the World Court, the International Court of Justice for example.
27. Malaysia does not just talk. We do. We settle disputes with our neighbours through negotiation and through the World Court. We won some and we lost some. But no one has been killed.
28. This talk about “not one inch of my territory” is ridiculous. We know that if we go to war, that inch is going to cost us more than what it is worth.
29. When one goes to court one does not always get what one claims to be rightfully ours. But it is the same with war. We do not always win. In a contest between two parties, one must lose if the other is to win. But if we use peaceful means we can still lose but it will cost us much less. No one would die, nor land devastated.
CLIMATE CHANGE AND CATASTROPHIES
30. The world is experiencing climate change. Malaysia is hotter than ever before. It does not seem to return to previous temperatures. In fact, it seems to be getting hotter.
31. Elsewhere powerful typhoons and hurricanes are destroying whole towns, killing thousands, wreaking havoc of unprecedented proportions. Flood waters from storms inundate huge areas of land. Sometimes there would be a dry spell and wild fires would destroy forest and towns. Hundreds would die.
32. Earthquakes and volcanic eruptions are more frequent and they destroy towns and cities. Melting snow in the Arctic and Antarctic is raising the levels of the seas and threaten to overrun islands.
33. I have a feeling that these disasters are a part of the cycles of change that our planet has been going through for millions of years. Can it be that the stable salubrious climate that we have been enjoying has come to the end of its cycle? Could it be that the cycle is changing, as it did in prehistoric millions of years? Is it possible that the temperatures rise to a level that living conditions would become unbearable?
34. I think, instead of preparing for war, we should be paying attention to the climate changes and accompanying natural disasters. We should be preparing to combat climate change, to bring back the normal environment we had been used to over the last thousands of years. We should be preparing ourselves for major earthquakes, typhoons and hurricanes, floods and landslides etc. We should learn how to mitigate these natural disasters. We should be constructing shelters, make rain and grow food without sunlight, evacuate the sea side etc. etc.
35. We should have teams of well equipped disaster experts ready to rush to disaster areas. Every disaster is a world disaster.
36. All these natural disasters may not happen of course. But we cannot rely on that. We are wasting our money preparing for wars, inventing ever more destructive weapons, when all of us may be wiped out by natural disasters as the planet goes through its next cycle.
37. We, the human creatures are clever. We can still survive the next cycle if we set our researchers to come up with defences against catastrophes. If we reduce our budget for killing people, we will have the funds for research and preparation.
TRADE, SANCTIONS AND CAPITALISM
38. Malaysia is a middle-income country. It depends on trade to grow. Naturally our markets are the rich countries.
39. Now the rich want us to balance the trade, to buy more of their goods, to correct the imbalance. To do this we will have to spend the money we earn from trade to import the goods of the rich. Our growth will be stunted so that the already rich will become richer.
40. Trade enriches everyone. It has been shown through the ages. Malaysia is a trading nation. Our population is too small to provide a good market. We need the world market. With the new communication technologies, we can increase our trade with the world. So, don’t impoverish us by forcing us to buy what we don’t need or to reduce our exports.
41. Trade wars are wasteful. Now that the whole world has become a market for everyone, trade wars will stultify the potential for everyone to become rich.
42. We are also seeing sanctions being applied to countries. We do not know under what laws sanctions are applied. It appears to be the privilege of the rich and the powerful. If we want to have sanctions, let us have a law to govern them. The fact is that when sanction is applied to a country, other countries get sanctioned as well. Malaysia and many others lost a big market when sanction is applied on Iran.
THE UNITED NATIONS - THE WAY FORWARD
43. I believe in capitalism. But capitalism has gone mad. They are already talking of making trillions. It is dangerous for a person or a company to have so much money. It can influence things. It can buy power. Hence the anti-trust laws. We see in the Trans Pacific Partnership – TPP, when the rich companies had given themselves the power to sue Governments. The terms of the agreements were drawn up by them. And they are not all like Bill Gates. Most are bent on exploiting the power money gives them.
44. The UN has failed in protecting the poor from the scourge of war. But in other fields it has done much better. It has contributed to better health, to alleviating the sufferings of some of the poor and the needy. It does provide a degree of security and stability in places plagued by internal conflicts.
45. It can do more. But it is short of funds. Countries including the very rich are not paying their dues. It is shameful.
46. We need to support the UN even though it has failed to banish wars. Its work on health, education and social security make the UN worth having.
47. I would like to thank the staff and officers of the UN for their work and dedication, in all these fields. Malaysia has been able to contribute by doing peace-keeping tasks in many countries. I look forward to the time when their services will no longer be needed, when countries are able to ensure their own security.
48. The UN should play a major role in the restoration of failed governments. Many countries have failed because the administrative machinery does not function well. Modern technology can help but there is a need for good training.
49. Countries and people should be allowed to retain their cultures and ways of life. Only if the way of life involves taking away the rights of people should there be international interference sanctioned by the UN General Assembly.
50. As for the UN Security Council, the time has come when the veto power should be modified if it cannot be done away with completely. The veto should only be valid if two Veto Powers together with three non-Veto members agree to apply it. That way abuses would be less frequent.
51. Three quarters of a century is a long time. We cannot be held to ransom by events of the distant past. The veto powers should not think they would always be above international laws and norms. Now – new, cheap but powerful weapons have been invented which even the poor can produce and use. If we do not make wars a crime our security cannot be sustained.
52. We must resuscitate the original purpose of this great organisation – the United Nations Organisation. We must punish warmongers. We must make the world peaceful for all. That was our mission and that must remain our mission. Only if we succeed can we claim that we are civilised. I thank you.",somewhat populist
gpd_Malaysia_Mohamad_Ribbon_1,Malaysia_Mohamad_Ribbon_1.txt,speeches_20251120/Malaysia_Mohamad_Ribbon_1.txt,Malaysia,Mahathir Mohamad,1,Ribbon cutting,2018,East Asia & Pacific,2,0.1,0.1,1201,2743,"TEKS UCAPAN YAB TUN DR MAHATHIR BIN MOHAMAD, PERDANA MENTERI MALAYSIA
MAJLIS MAKAN MALAM SEMPENA SAMBUTAN 60 TAHUN PARLIMEN MALAYSIA PADA 4 DISEMBER 2019 (RABU), JAM 8.30 MALAM BERTEMPAT DI PARLIMEN MALAYSIA PENDAHULUAN
1. Saya sangat bersyukur kerana diberi kesempatan bersama-sama ahli-ahli Yang Berhormat serta pegawai dan kakitangan Parlimen bagi meraikan majlis makan malam sempena sambutan 60 Tahun Parlimen Malaysia.
2. Pada usia 60 tahun Parlimen Malaysia telah berjaya untuk terus kekal sebagai institusi dan simbol demokrasi serta mewakili suara dan kuasa rakyat.
3. Ianya satu pencapaian yang bukan sahaja membanggakan tetapi perlu dipertahankan selagi kita berpegang kepada amalan demokrasi dan yakin bahawa suara rakyat itu suara keramat.
4. Sambutan ini juga amat bermakna kerana ia diraikan setahun selepas kemenangan Pakatan Harapan pada Pilihan Raya Umum Malaysia ke-14.
5. Walaupun berlaku perubahan dari segi parti yang menerajui Kerajaan buat pertama kalinya sejak Merdeka, namun tradisi dan amalan demokrasi terdahulu tetap diteruskan dan dipertahankan, dan di mana perlu, kita perbaiki. MENGURUS DEMOKRASI
6. Sistem Demokrasi Berparlimen dan Raja Berpelembagaan yang kita amalkan selama lebih 60 tahun ini telah memberi kuasa kepada rakyat dalam memilih Kerajaan yang akan memerintah.
7. Dalam tempoh pemerintahan yang diamanahkan untuk satu penggal tidak melebihi 5 tahun, Kerajaan yang dipilih tidak boleh memerintah sesuka hati tanpa mengambil kira kepentingan rakyat. Jika kuasa yang diamanahkan itu disalahguna dan membawa keburukan kepada rakyat ataupun untuk kepentingan peribadi, Kerajaan akan dihukum seperti yang kita telah saksi di dalam pilihanraya yang lalu.
8. Proses peralihan kuasa yang berlaku secara aman tanpa adanya rusuhan atau keganasan membuktikan Sistem Demokrasi Berparlimen dan Raja Berpelembagaan yang kita amalkan dilaksanakan dengan agak berjaya.
9. Walaupun terdapat rasa tidak puas hati di kalangan segelintir rakyat berkaitan amalan demokrasi kita terutamanya kerana kewujudan beberapa undang-undang yang dianggap bertentangan dengan semangat demokrasi itu sendiri, Kerajaan yang baik akan sentiasa berusaha untuk memperbaiki di mana perlu. Embargo Please check against delivery 2
10. Janji-janji yang terdapat di dalam Manifesto Pilihanraya Pakatan Harapan turut menekankan akan keperluan tersebut kita telah menunaikan beberapa janji tersebut dan yang lain di dalam proses untuk dipenuhi. MEMPERTAHANKAN DEMOKRASI
11. Sistem demokrasi adalah sesuatu yang hidup dan berterusan. Undang-undang yang kita perkenalkan pada satu masa dahulu kerana keperluan semasa terpaksa kita pinda dan adakala dimansuh kerana sudah tidak relevan atau tidak sesuai dengan amalan dan semangat demokrasi masa kini.
12. Pada Julai 2019, Negara juga mencipta sejarah baharu, apabila pindaan Perlembagaan Persekutuan bagi menurunkan had umur kelayakan mengundi kepada 18 tahun diluluskan dengan sokongan 211 daripada 222 ahli Parlimen. Pindaan ini akan meningkatkan jumlah pengundi baru lebih 50 peratus pada tahun 2023 iaitu sekitar 22.7 juta pengundi berbanding hanya 14.9 juta pada Pilihan Raya Umum ke-14.
13. Kerajaan juga dalam proses untuk menyemak dan meminda undang-undang yang kita anggap bertentangan dengan semangat demokrasi dan ini akan terus berjalan dan dilaksanakan. AMANAH YANG DITUNTUT
14. Malaysia baharu yang terbina lebih daripada setahun lalu menuntut pembaharuan dan reformasi besar dalam semua segi, bukan sahaja pengurusan pentadbiran Kerajaan, politik dan cara berpolitik, malah perwatakan kita sebagai Wakil Rakyat juga perlu diubah.
15. Kuasa yang diamanahkan kepada Kerajaan oleh rakyat bukan sesuatu untuk kita bermegah-megah tetapi menjadi tanggungjawab kita untuk melaksanakan amanah tersebut dengan penuh integriti, adil dan saksama.
16. Jika mahu dipercayai dan dihormati, jangan lakukan perkara-perkara yang merendahkan martabat kita dan pamerkan sifat-sifat yang baik dan idea-idea konstruktif yang boleh membawa kepada sesuatu kejayaan.
17. Ahli politik perlu mengamalkan politik yang beretika dan berhujah dengan fakta yang betul. Setiap perkara yang dibahaskan dan apa jua tindakan yang akan dilaksanakan haruslah berlandaskan kejujuran dan kebijaksanaan, elakkan berpolitik dengan pemikiran yang sempit dan penuh kebencian. REFORMASI PARLIMEN
18. Reformasi Parlimen yang dilaksanakan tidak akan berjalan dengan baik tanpa kerjasama dan sokongan semua ahli-ahli Parlimen.
19. Ahli-ahli Parlimen seharusnya merebut peluang untuk mengisi proses reformasi ini sebaik mungkin. Kita juga perlu bersedia mengubah cara lama kita bekerja dan perlu lebih rajin mendalami ilmu-ilmu baru selari dengan keperluan proses reformasi yang dilaksanakan.
20. Walaupun kita terbahagi antara ahli Parlimen Kerajaan dan pembangkang, adakala kita perlu bertindak secara bi-partisan kerana kita tahun ianya adalah untuk kebaikan rakyat. Embargo Please check against delivery 3
21. Adakala kita lupa terhadap tanggungjawab kita kepada rakyat dan terus mempertahankan yang batil atas dasar setia sedangkan kita tahu kesalahan telah dilaku yang merugikan rakyat.
22. Penubuhan Jawatankuasa Pilihan Khas Parlimen memberi peluang kepada ahli-ahli Parlimen untuk bertindak dengan lebih fokus dalam menyemak pelaksanaan sesuatu dasar, undang-undang atau rancangan pembangunan Negara. Kita percaya cadangan dan idea yang dihasilkan boleh membantu Kerajaan melaksanakan dasar dan perancangan Negara dengan lebih baik. HARAPAN KEPADA AHLI PARLIMEN MUDA
23. Parlimen hari ini terdiri daripada ramai ahli-ahli yang muda (berumur di bawah 45 tahun). Mereka mewakili 25 peratus ahli di Dewan Rakyat dan 15 peratus ahli Dewan Negara. Proses Reformasi Parlimen akan lebih bermakna dengan penglibatan aktif mereka.
24. Pendedahan dan kemahiran mereka dalam bidang teknologi maklumat menjadikan mereka golongan lebih bermaklumat dan seharusnya membantu proses pemikiran yang lebih jelas dan matang. Oleh itu mereka ini harus diberi peluang, ruang dan suara untuk bersama-sama berganding bahu membangunkan Negara.
25. Dalam memberi peluang kita juga menuntut golongan muda hari ini mengamalkan nilainilai murni dan membina jati diri sebagai anak Malaysia. Nilai-nilai integriti dan bencikan rasuah perlu diserap menjadi sebahagian budaya hidup mereka.
26. Ini kerana masalah rasuah di kalangan anak muda sangat membimbangkan. Kajian Transparency International menunjukkan 66 peratus anak muda di rantau Asia Pacific bersedia menerima rasuah sekiranya berpeluang. Statistik daripada Suruhanjaya Pencegahan Rasuah Malaysia (SPRM) dari 2014 hingga 2019, menunjukan sebanyak 53.4 peratus daripada tangkapan kes rasuah Negara adalah melibatkan golongan muda yang berumur di bawah 40 tahun. INTEGRITI DAN TADBIR URUS YANG BAIK
27. Kerajaan Pakatan Harapan yang terbentuk hari ini adalah hasil dari penolakan rakyat terhadap sebuah Kerajaan yang mengamalkan rasuah dan bersifat kleptokrasi. Adalah menjadi komitmen Kerajaan untuk memulihkan imej negara agar Malaysia dikenali sebagai sebuah Negara berintegriti dan bebas rasuah.
28. Kerajaan sedar perlakuan rasuah di kalangan sektor awam boleh memusnahkan negara. Kajian SPRM bagi tempoh 2013 hingga 2018, sebanyak 63.3 peratus aduan rasuah yang diterima oleh SPRM adalah melibatkan sektor awam dan sektor awam juga dikenalpasti paling terdedah kepada gejala rasuah.
29. Untuk itu, pada Januari 2019, Kerajaan telah memperkenalkan Pelan Anti-Rasuah National (National Anti-Corruption Plan – NACP) untuk menangani gejala rasuah dengan mempromosikan urus tadbir yang baik iaitu mengamalkan sikap telus, berintegriti dan bertanggungjawab di semua pentadbiran Kerajaan.
30. Sebagai badan perundangan tertinggi Negara adalah menjadi harapan Kerajaan agar dapat melihat Pelan Anti-Rasuah Parlimen dilaksanakan secepat mungkin agar Institusi Parlimen bebas rasuah dan politik Negara lebih berintegriti. Embargo Please check against delivery 4 PENUTUP
31. Kerajaan sedar perpaduan rakyat adalah kunci kejayaan membina semula Negara. Untuk itu Wawasan Kemakmuran Bersama 2030 (WKB2030) telah dibangunkan bagi mengukuh kestabilan politik dan meningkatkan kemakmuran Negara berasaskan penyatuan Negara bangsa.
32. Pelbagai inisiatif yang telah dirancang dan dilaksanakan Kerajaan tidak akan tercapai tanpa kerjasama dan sokongan semua pihak. Saya menyeru kepada semua ahli-ahli Parlimen untuk membangunkan Negara demi kesejahteraan dan kemakmuran rakyat, walaupun kita berbeza dari segi fahaman politik.
33. Akhir kata, saya mengucapkan tahniah kepada pihak Parlimen Malaysia kerana berjaya mengadakan majlis makan malam sempena sambutan 60 tahun Parlimen Malaysia dan terima kasih juga kerana memberi kesempatan kepada saya untuk memberi ucapan ini.
Sekian. Wabillahhi Taufik Walhidayah Wassalamualaikum Warahmatullahi Wabarakatuh.",not populist
gpd_Malaysia_Razak_Campaign_1,Malaysia_Razak_Campaign_1.txt,speeches_20251120/Malaysia_Razak_Campaign_1.txt,Malaysia,Najib Tun Razak,1,Campaign,2009,East Asia & Pacific,2,0.05,0.050000001,5985,7157,"Name of Politician: Najib Razak
Title of Speech: Speech by YAB Dato’ Sri Mohd Najib Bin Tun Abd Razak at the Opening of the Joint Assembly of Wanita, Pemuda and Puteri UMNO 2009
Date of Speech: 3/24/2009

SPEECH BY YAB DATO' SRI MOHD NAJIB BIN TUN HJ ABD RAZAK DEPUTY PRESIDENT OF UMNO AT THE OPENING OF THE JOINT ASSEMBLY OF WANITA, PEMUDA AND PUTERI UMNO 2009 8.30 P.M. 24TH MARCH, 2009, MERDEKA HALL, PUTRA WORLD TRADE CENTER KUALA LUMPUR ---------------------------------------- Bismillahirrahmanirrahim [SALUTATIONS]

Delegates and observers,

Praise be to Allah, let us all give thanks to the Almighty for his Grace in allowing us to congregate here tonight.

First of all we would like to congratulate Wanita, Pemuda and Puteri UMNO for having successfully exercised their responsibility in convening their branch and divisional meetings

Indeed Wanita Pemuda and Puteri are respectively the backbone and the wings of UMNO. The rise and fall, the success or failure of the party depends on all of you, the members of our party. With great drive and tenacity, Wanita, Pemuda and Puteri must strive with great commitment to act as a force which ignites the torch of our struggle. Have not the slightest doubt that this road upon which we have chosen to travel is an honorable one.

Recently we went through two by-elections namely the Permatang Pauh parliamentary by-election followed by the Kuala Terengganu parliamentary by-election. Even though in both cases fate was not on our side, I would like to record my appreciation to Wanita, Pemuda and Puteri for displaying a spirited show of force. We fully believe that the same great spirit and confidence will come forth once again for all three by-elections which we will face on April 7th.
Ladies and gentlemen,

This is the first Assembly for us since the 12th General Elections on March 8th, 2008. Clearly, the results of that General Election have been the worst in the history of our party. We lost the two-thirds majority in Parliament for the first time since Barisan Nasional was formed more than three decades ago. It is an awful and bitter truth, but a truth none the less and one which we must accept.

Whether we like it or not, we must acknowledge that what happened had very much to do with certain weaknesses which are prevalent within our party. To the perception of many, UMNO has swayed far from its original struggle and its raison d’être. Obviously there must have been a reason why a large number of the rakyat who once walked along side UMNO, have since changed their direction.

That being the case, your collective duty as General Assembly delegates this year is the heaviest duty to have ever been borne by any delegation in the history of UMNO. Starkly different from the party elections of previous years, at stake this year is not just a handful of party posts, nor is it a matter of positions or status for any individual. What is at stake is nothing less than the very fate of UMNO. The decision we collectively make at this assembly will determine the future of our party; whether we continue to shape and mould history, or just become an entry in the annals of history.

The fact remains that UMNO is still very much loved by the Malays. No one can deny this. It is because of this that they have voted to retain UMNO as the biggest party with the most number of seats in the Dewan Rakyat even though a two-thirds majority was denied. What is painfully clear is that UMNO must learn from the message that was conveyed to them by the Malays (through the ballot box). If we do not heed this message, their seething anger will become hatred and in the end this may cause them to abandon us altogether.
Ladies and gentlemen,

As Muslims, when we face any challenge or difficulty, it is best that we return to the teachings of our religion. Let us look at the following three verses of the Holy Quran as guidance.
Verse 26 of the surah Ali Imran reads as follows: “Say: ""O Allah. Lord of Power (And Rule), Thou givest power to whom Thou pleasest, and Thou strippest off power from whom Thou pleasest: Thou enduest with honour whom Thou pleasest, and Thou bringest low whom Thou pleases..” In the Surah Ar-Ra’d verse 11, Allah says: For each (such person) there are (angels) in succession, before and behind him: They guard him by command of Allah. Verily never will Allah change the condition of a people until they change it themselves (with their own souls). Whereas in the Surah Az-Zumar, verse 53, it is written: Say: ""O my Servants who have transgressed against their souls! Despair not of the Mercy of Allah. for Allah forgives all sins: for He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.

Taking lessons from those holy verses, we gather here tonight not to wallow in sadness nor to lament our fate. But as a party, we are here today but for one singular purpose, that is to chart the way forward for UMNO and our struggle.

The wise have often said, we must first examine history and at the same time evaluate the present in order for us to be able to forecast the future. History has shown that in the sixty three years it has been in existence, UMNO has contributed greatly for the development of the nation and her people. UMNO was a leading force in the successful fight for independence. Such was the monumental achievement when UMNO carried the will of the people and the aspirations of the masses.

In those heady days of seeking self rule, realizing that independence cannot be meaningful if the Malays worked alone, the UMNO leadership wisely laid the foundation for an enduring power sharing formula amongst all the major races. To the fulfillment of that formula, UMNO made great sacrifices in the first General Election of 1955 when it agreed to allow Malay majority constituencies to be represented by non-Malay parties. That noble sacrifice has become UMNO’s tradition and is still practiced until today.
Ladies and gentlemen,

The achievements of UMNO in more than six decades of existence, is by no means small or insignificant. It did not end with the attainment of Independence, but rather continued with and unparalleled record of excellence in nation building. UMNO members should be proud of this and should never be apologetic when faced with the empty rhetoric and baseless accusations of opposition parties.

(First Decade Post Independence 1957-1970) In the political developments of our country, UMNO has never stood as a mere observer in the sidelines of history but instead has always played a pro-active role in carving and shaping the path for the nation and the people. Immediately after the Emergency in the first decade of independence, was it not UMNO that launched a war against poverty, and opened up new lands through the Felda land settlement schemes and through the development of rural areas?

(Second Decade Post Independence 1971-1980) In the second decade after Independence, when the people’s unhappiness manifested itself in the tragedy of May 13th 1969, was it not the UMNO leadership that quickly acted to identify the causes of the problem and unveiled the New Economic Policy? It was the NEP that successfully created a substantial Malay middle class and became the foundation for Malaysia’s economic growth for the next three decades.

(Third Decade Post Independence 1981-1990) In the third decade after Independence, when we were hit by an economic slump following the collapse of commodity prices, was it not UMNO’s leadership that launched the industrialization initiative and a wide-scale infrastructure development program to modernize the country?

(Fourth Decade Post Independence 1991-2000) Following that, in the fourth decade of nationhood, was it not UMNO’s leadership that unveiled the Vision 2020 as a basis to catapult the nation into the era of information technology and globalization? In the financial crisis of 1997 and 1998, was it not UMNO that saved Malaysia from spiraling into the quagmire of the Asian economic crisis? Indeed we even found our own way out of the crisis, using our own formula and without need for recourse to the IMF. Ironically, the way we dealt with the crisis back then is today a template that is being followed by the very same countries that had roundly condemned our approach.

Praise be to Allah. UMNO has clearly proven to be a party that brings hope in place of misery. It has also been proven that UMNO is a party that is capable of building a proud and civilized nation that is respected the world over. It is this party that has done so much to uplift the lives of Malaysians, extricating them from the clutches of poverty and elevating them to higher quality of life in just one generation. Let there be no doubt that it is this great party that leads the way forward. UMNO has always been and must always be a Leader of the Times.
Ladies and gentlemen,

Having said that, I must add that UMNO members must have their feet on the ground, no matter what our achievements have been in the past. We cannot just remain nostalgic about past glory and fail to record new accomplishments and successes. The political landscape of this country has completely changed. To remain relevant, we have no choice but to move with the times.

Looking at the demographics, we find that more than one third of the Malaysian population can be categorized as ‘Youth’ i.e. they are within the 15-40 age group. More than 70 percent of those below 40 were born after the tragedy of May 13, 1969. Overall, 90 percent of the population were born post Merdeka. whereas those born after the end of the NEP, i.e. those born in 1991, will be eligible to vote by the year 2012

These changes, coupled with advances in ICT, greater accessibility and mobility, economic progress and better education have directly resulted in the birth of a class of voters who are better informed, very demanding and highly critical. We must always remember that this generation may not be able to relate to the past struggles of our party because they were never there and they only learn of past events from books and stories.

This is not to suggest that the struggles of the past are therefore no longer important. But it demands that we once again assume the role of the leaders of change in our effort to fulfill aspirations, especially those of the Malays. To that end, there must be some introspection on our part followed by renewal and rejuvenation. It is clear that our advancement is conditional upon our ability to correctly asses our strengths and weaknesses. Weaknesses must be addressed whereas strengths should be further amplified. If we do not undertake this process UMNO will continue to be seen as a party still in denial. This effort to reinvigorate the party demands that we revive the ideals of our struggle.

To do this UMNO must first remove itself from being linked to “money politics’ and any other form of unsavory activities. UMNO, or for that matter any party or organization will be destroyed if its leaders are enshrouded in the evils of money politics. Leaders of good standing who do not indulge in corruption will be sidelined in favour of those who bribe. The party will be led by those who will bring their culture of corruption in the way they lead.

Clearly if this evil is not halted and is allowed to grow and fester, it will become so commonplace that leaders and followers alike can make light of it with humorous remarks like “ beri salah, tak beri kalah” (To give would be wrong, not to give would result in defeat). This is no laughing matter. We must resolve to eradicate money politics right down to the roots. If not, we will all be collectively responsible for the demise of this beloved party of ours.
Ladies and gentlemen,

UMNO cannot afford to be seen as a party that is resistant to new ideas and new people or a party that does not welcome the young. In actual fact, we are the political party that has been credited with increasing access to education especially at tertiary level. Now 38 percent of those in the 17-23 age group have access to higher education. This is expected to rise to 40 percent by 2010, and 50 percent by 2020. These well educated youngsters are the product of UMNO’s effort and we cannot sit back and just allow them to be enticed by others. We must capture their imagination and convince them that our party moves in line with their aspirations.

We must ensure that we as a party cease and desist from the deplorable acts of eliminating and blocking talented members from making progress in the party. Such despicable behaviour only serves to alienate those who sincerely wish to contribute to the struggle. If this goes on unchecked, it will spell the beginning of the end for this glorious party that has for so long served as the backbone of the people and the nation.

Apart from that, whether we realize it or not, there is now a perception that the aspirations of UMNO are far removed from the aspirations of the masses. To those having this perception, they feel that what UMNO wants is very different from what the rakyat expects. As such we must correct this perception and we must not get trapped in our own cocoon. We mustn’t get too caught up in the internal processes of the party. We must never be too preoccupied with winning positions in the party, to the extent that we forget that the real measure of success of a democratic political party is whether or not it can win elections. Indeed, what is the point of winning party positions within a party that is bereft of authority and is no longer in power?

Furthermore, we know that not all Malays are members of UMNO. It follows that UMNO will become stronger if it opens its doors to as many Malays as possible and if it continues to be the party that represents their aspirations. UMNO will be truly great if the culture of humility and readiness to serve is embraced by all its members. UMNO will be more resilient if UMNO members stop asking what they can get from the party, but instead ask what they can give to the religion, race and nation through UMNO.

Therefore it is imperative that we shed and discard the image and perception that UMNO’s leaders are elitist and out of touch with the people. UMNO leaders must be adept at interpreting the needs and wants of the people and in understanding the developments in the community. Let us not forget our roots. Let us remember that UMNO is a grassroots party, a party that was born from the will and spirit of the masses wanting to affect change. Understand that on our shoulders we bear the heavy burden of nothing less than the fate of our people.

If indeed we have floundered from the soul and spirit of the origins of UMNO’s struggles, then let us change and go back where we were before. Let us put UMNO back on track. To do this we need leaders who are able and are themselves enablers, leaders who dare to change and are accepting of change; who dare to criticize and are willing to accept criticism.
Ladies and gentlemen,

As the biggest of all of UMNO’s wings, Wanita UMNO under the leadership of Tan Sri Rafidah Aziz has displayed unwavering commitment whatever the circumstances, especially each time we face election. The unity of Wanita is extremely important for UMNO. Therefore let us not forsake all that we have achieved thus far just because of a temporary excitement over contests for party posts. We do not want to see disunity. Be united, for indeed the winner does not take all and the loser does not lose all. The victor must be magnanimous and accept the vanquished with an open heart. The vanquished must accept the decision of the delegates and continue with the struggles of the party.

To Pemuda UMNO, you are the warriors who safeguard the party. Pemuda have always been at the forefront of our struggles. The last decade that has been so fraught with difficulties saw Pemuda steadfastly guarding the party. On this occasion allow me to record my highest appreciation to Datuk Sri Hishamuddin Tun Hussein who has successfully led Pemuda from an era of uncertainty to one of stability and then displaying leadership and commitment in supporting the ideals of the struggle for more than a decade.

The same also goes for Puteri UMNO which we formed almost a decade ago. Puteri has successfully ignited the interest of young women to be involved in mainstream politics. I thank Datuk Noraini Ahmad for a job well done throughout her tenure as the leader of Puteri UMNO. What is important here is that we wish to see Puteri continue working hard as an important element that refreshes and brings rejuvenation to the party.
Ladies and gentlemen,

This assembly marks the handing over of the torch of the party’s struggle to a new generation of leaders. The invaluable experience of the first 50 years after Independence shall serve as guidance for the next 50 years to come. However in order for UMNO to remain current and relevant, it must be borne in mind that the second 50 years after Independence will be very different from what we have been used to. UMNO leaders must ensure that they remain ahead of the curve and not become mere reactionary followers. This entails a careful reevaluation and re-examination of the attitudes and value systems of the members of UMNO.

For a simple example, let us look back at the elections of 1999, when the New Media first appeared as an influential forum. We took it lightly and paid very little heed to that development. Five years later in 2004, we still paid very little attention to the importance of the alternative media. We were lulled by the massive mandate given to us to the extent that we made no preparations for battle within the cyber sphere. In the end we were rudely awakened in 2008 when we suddenly realized the folly of not understanding the power of the new media.

Like it or not, we cannot regard the new media as our enemy. The new generation of UMNO leaders must be active participants in this important development. The younger generation of UMNO must be able to speak the language of the cyber community. They must also be leaders in the utilization of technology as an essential part of our political arsenal. Only then can we win in the battle of ideas and influence in the arena of politics.
Ladies and gentlemen,

In the tradition of Malay Muslims, when we find that we have lost our way, we are taught to return to the beginning through the process of reflection and introspection. Therefore in honour of the month of the birth of the Holy Prophet Muhammad (P.B.U.H), let us take lessons from his history and experience as the greatest transformational leader of all time. He successfully led and educated the pagan Arabs from a period of darkness into the age of enlightenment.

During the Hijrah (Exodus from Makkah to Medinah), he united the tribes of Auz and Khazraj, and subsequently he brought together as one the Muhajireen and the Ansar. Later he proceeded to unite the Muslims and the non-Muslims. All this was done because the Hole Prophet understood the importance of unity as the foundation of strength for the city of Medinah at that point in history. This goes to show that the success and failure of a certain civilization depends not just on physical developments alone. Rather there are more important elements like unity and solidarity which comes from emotional and spiritual factors as well as the value system of a particular community and its leadership.

Among the most important values that will determine the success or failure of any peoples are the values of comradeship, discipline, respect for time, honoring one’s word, dedication to work, efficiency in the implementation of tasks, diligence and the placement of the interest of the larger community over and above the interests of the individual. Indeed these are the universal values of Islam that the Holy Prophet has enjoined in leading the ummah towards success and glory.

History has shown that Malays are greatly respected when they adhere steadfastly to the teachings of Islam. With the history of the Muslim Civilization as a guidance, we must understand that in the name of survival we must undertake a complete transformation that is total and tangible. Looking back at history, we can only conclude that national unity must first begin with Malay unity. Unfortunately, Malay unity today is being torn asunder day after day by the deplorable culture of spreading hatred through slander, the spreading of half truths and the fabrication of horrible lies. Today, slander is not just practice of the hypocrites (Munafiq), but sadly it has become a norm for individuals claiming to be Muslim leaders and religious scholars.

Looking at this situation, UMNO as the political platform for the Malays must correct its mission and direction and it must identify new and refreshing initiatives to transform UMNO in order to re-claim its position as the party of choice for all Malays.

Towards the fulfillment of this objective it is important for us to improve the way we train and educate our political cadres. At all levels, members of UMNO must be given sufficient training and education so that they fully understand the history of the party’s struggles. Only then can we foster loyalty predicated on the full belief in what UMNO stands for. This is not something we can take lightly for history has shown its importance in determining the success or failure of a particular civilization. Therefore we must strengthen the political training and education of our members through well planned courses, carried out in stages and based on a carefully crafted curriculum which emphasizes history, self-confidence and espirit de corps.

We would like to suggest that leadership training in the form of 3-day 2 night courses or 4-day 3 night courses be carried out at camps or training centers across the country. The modules for such training ought to focus on the strengthening of values aimed at creating honorable future leaders. The training should also include stints in the jungles or the sea, not only to toughen up the trainees but also to foster greater camaraderie and brotherhood among UMNO members and party leaders.

Secondly we must change the way UMNO chooses it leaders including reexamining the quota system. We must give the right to choose the leaders to a greater number of members. As it stands, the deciders are a delegation of some 2600 delegates from 191 divisions. Clearly the choice of these delegates cannot correctly reflect the preferences of more than 3 million grassroots members from across the nation. To my mind, the time has come for us to review the Constitution of UMNO regarding this matter so that the selection of UMNO leaders will be more inclusive of a greater number of UMNO members from all levels.

This move will be able to put to an end the problems of money politics and abuse of power. This is the path we must take if we are to regain our strength by returning to the grassroots the mandate for choosing party leaders. When the people are with us, UMNO will regain its full-strength once again. And we can accomplish this if each and every member and leader in UMNO embraces the passion for service to the people. Every problem that we resolve for the people, every difficulty that we ease, every complication that we unravel for our constituents ought to serve as reward and encouragement enough for us to continue to serve.
Ladies and gentlemen,

Today, about two-thirds of the Malaysian population live in urban areas. On the back of successful development policies created by UMNO, many among the Malays have now chosen to become urban dwellers, seeking better opportunities in cities and towns. Unfortunately not all of them have done well and there are families from the lower income group in the cities who find it difficult to even make ends meet. In light of this, UMNO must now not only focus its fight to end poverty in rural areas, but also in urban areas.

UMNO divisions in the cities must play their part in helping the lower-income urban Malays. It is our proud record to have been able to eradicate hardcore poverty in the rural areas through various programs and initiatives. Now it is time for us to shift our focus towards addressing the real problem of urban poverty. UMNO as one of the core parties in the ruling coalition will ensure that the eradication of urban poverty is given top priority by the government.
Ladies and gentlemen,

UMNO holds sacred the position of the Federal Constitution as the supreme law of the land. The Malay rulers and the Monarchy are an essential part of the Constitution. Even though in our system the Monarch reigns but does not rule, the state governments and the federal government rule in the name of the Malay rulers as the head above the executive arm of government. Therefore if the Malays themselves fail to show the utmost respect to Malay Rulers who have all this time served as the symbol of unity and stability, then who else will?

Therefore let no one twist the facts of history in recounting UMNO’s actions to amend the law with regard to the Rulers. It was never done in bad faith, but rather with the noble intention of preserving the Royal Institution and upholding the doctrine of the separation of powers which is the basis of any democratic government. I wish to take this opportunity to remind all Malays not to do things which we might regret later. To those who speak with a forked tongue, do not pledge allegiance in the morning only to betray by mid afternoon.
Ladies and gentlemen,

With all the national and global challenges that we face, we are fast running out of time. The global economic crisis that we now face is far beyond anyone’s expectations and is in fact the worst crisis since The Great Depression. Therefore we cannot afford to be lulled into a false sense of security and divorce ourselves from the stark realities that plague the world. Malaysia’s economy today is very different from our economy of 50 years ago. Today we are among the top 20 trading nations of the world with trade in a year valued at more than one trillion ringgit.

We cannot avoid feeling some of the effects of what has happened to the global economy. The prosperity that we enjoy today is greatly linked to the state of the rest of the world. We will find it difficult to progress if the global economy continues to slide. But more importantly, we cannot recover if there is no confidence from the people. In fact, a precondition of economic recovery is political stability and a nation strongly united. And so in these trying times let us put aside petty differences and see the bigger picture. Let us put the interest of the Rakyat over and above narrow political interests.
Ladies and gentlemen,

There is a Malay proverb that says “language is the soul of a people”. I wish to categorically state here that the special position of the Malay language will always be upheld no matter what happens. However, I would also like to remind all of us, that if a people perishes what good is the language of that people? Consider Latin after the collapse of Rome. It is now almost extinct but for ceremonial use in academic institutions and traditional ceremonies. Consider also Sanskrit, and the Incan and Aztec languages all of which have perished with the extinction of the people who speak them. The more important consideration is strengthening the people or the race that speaks the language. Indeed, who would care to learn a language of a people who are weak, poor and lacking in knowledge?

As such, the continuity of a particular language largely depends on the strength of the people to whom the language belongs. Only a people of great strength and high standing will raise the dignity of their own language, their culture and their value system. And so the crux of the matter lies in strengthening the people or race, first and foremost. To do this, we must first master knowledge and wisdom, much of which is today documented in the English language. Therefore, our younger generation must master the English language. Not only that we must be proficient in at least three major languages in order to be able to truly shine in the global arena. Please have no fear. Learning another language does not diminish who we are as Malays. Instead it will make us stronger and increase our self confidence in facing the challenges of a globalized world.

Let us not waste any more time. Stop these pointless polemics. Put an end to the ridiculous politicizing of this issue. Let us all roll up our sleeves and harness the strengths of this great nation so that we can ensure her continuous progress and prosperity. Remember, UMNO is not just any political party like those of the opposition. We are a party entrusted by the people to spearhead the government. The people depend on us as a party that will provide leadership and solve their problems.

UMNO and the Malays can never be separated. Like the river and its bank, like a song and its melody. History has shown that when UMNO and the Malays move as one, we rose to far greater heights than we ever thought possible. But when we are in disarray to the extent that there are those who abandon the interest of the Malays for their own selfish gains, then that is when negative elements quickly seep in and fan the flames of discontent. Now, we see that the Malays seem lost and weakened. Because of that there are those who dare question what has previously been agreed to and entrenched in the Federal Constitution. There are even those who have the audacity to accuse us of Apartheid, when history will show this is far from the truth.

Let it be known, that the policies introduced by the government in aid of the Malays are not formulated because we feel that the Malays are better than everyone else. Rather, we create these policies precisely because the Malays are left behind compared to others. In fact, if we allow the Malays and the Bumiputera who form more than two thirds of our population fall by the wayside of progress, without any assistance or aid, then surely this is a formula for instability. At the end of the day, the policies of the government will always be anchored on the principle of fairness for all

For UMNO, it must remain relevant by continuing to win the hearts and minds of the Malays. Whether we like it or not, we must change for the benefit of the people. We must dare to change and abandon negative behaviour in favour of praiseworthy attributes. Change from being aloof to being friendly and approachable. Change from always thinking of our self interest to instead putting the interest of the people above our own. Change from laziness to diligence. Change from doing the required minimum to embracing a passion for service. We must change. For if we do not, we shall surely falter.
Ladies and gentlemen,

At this juncture I, on behalf of UMNO, would like to record my highest appreciation and thanks to the party President who has led the party for the past five years. YAB Dato' Seri Abdullah Hj Ahmad Badawi, in his effort to increase public confidence in the judiciary established the Judicial Appointments Commission. He also continued his effort to fight corruption by establishing the Malaysian Anti Corruption Commission.

We thank Pak Lah for his contributions, especially in providing a social safety net in terms of fighting hardcore poverty and strengthening the agricultural sector.

The foundation of all these initiatives was the emphasis by the Prime Minister on the importance of nurturing a strong pool of human capital. Pak Lah saw that half a century after we attained independence, we successfully built modern infrastructure of world class standards. All of that had to be complemented with competitive and highly skilled human capital. This effort to strengthen our human capital became a pillar of our National Mission, and we will continue this journey towards achieving our National Vision.
Ladies and gentlemen,

Looking back at my own personal political journey, it has been more than 33 years that I have been with the UMNO Wings, every time we converge for the General Assembly. It is with mixed emotions that I stand before you here tonight, speaking to all of you for the last time as Deputy President of the party. I am extremely moved by the notion that I have been entrusted with the faith and confidence of the grassroots lead the party and nation.

Indeed I am most humbled by the reality that this path of leadership upon which I am about to traverse was pioneered by the greatest of men. I stand on the shoulder of giants like Allahyarham Dato’ Onn Jaafar followed by Almarhum Tunku Abdul Rahman Putra Al Haj, who was later followed by my beloved father Allahyarham Tun Abdul Razak. He was followed by Allahyarham Tun Hussein Onn who was then succeeded by YABhg Tun Dr. Mahathir Mohamad. Now, the burden carried by YAB Dato' Seri Abdullah Ahmad Badawi will be handed over to me. And so in these most trying of times for the party and the country, I bear on my shoulders the enormous responsibility to continue UMNO’s struggle to fight of the betterment of the people.

I wish to sincerely record my personal thanks to each and every member of UMNO who have given me their support. And I wish to express my highest gratitude to Wanita, Pemuda and Puteri for giving me their fullest cooperation for the whole of my tenure as Deputy President of UMNO.

It is my hope that I will receive the same support and cooperation from all of you when I the time comes for me to assume the Presidency of the party. I also believe that the same support will be given to the new Deputy President of UMNO who will be elected soon. I greatly believe that if we al stand shoulder to shoulder and work hand in hand, there will be no burden we cannot carry, no hurdle we cannot surmount as we work together to lead the times.

Finally, I implore you to give me a line of leaders who are strong and able. Present to me a team that has the traits of loyalty, integrity, ability and dedication to duty. I pray to Allah that the voice of UMNO’s struggles will continue to reverberate in these hallowed halls. Whatever the challenges may come our way, we shall face it all unflinchingly and together, with great determination we will reach the highest summit.

In the name of Allah, the most Gracious, most Merciful, I hereby officially open the Joint Assembly of Wanita, Pemuda and Puteri UMNO 2008.",not populist
